## Data accuracy

Manifests are generated from the local Steam client caches on a machine with a
pristine install, and cross-validated against the byte totals Steam records in
`appmanifest_<appid>.acf`. Each manifest's SHA-256 is recorded in
`manifests/registry.json` and verified on every load.

Even so: a manifest describes **one specific build**. If a game has been
updated, patch your manifest rather than assuming tampering. Verify the
manifest digest against a second, independent source before drawing security
conclusions from a scan.
